in @prism
in @meta
in @glass
in @aikido
in @mirror/reflection

# @aikido/reflect — Tier-1 aikido response species; the substrate-decl
# for consent-through-refusal via @mirror/reflection dispatch.
#
# Species under @aikido at Tier-1 altitude (default response). Landed
# 2026-07-20 by Mara Round-3 per Alex Round-3 spawn brief §Tier 1.6.
#
# === The species altitude ===
#
# Tier 1 of the aikido runtime loop (per shards/aikido.mirror §The
# three-tier response surface): the DEFAULT response mode when the
# @cyberpunk/algedonic threshold is BELOW Tier-1 escalation boundary.
# Corresponds to aikido's `irimi` (entering — meeting the incoming
# momentum without countering it).
#
# The Tier-1 discipline: reflect the incoming question back as a
# witnessed answer WITHOUT accepting the embedded frame. The peer
# metabolizes the question via @mirror/reflection's three-operation
# discipline (mirror + offer + wait per Alex Wolf's 2026-07-14
# "Weird - Violence" manifesto three-word closing incantation:
# "Mirror. Offer. Wait. 🍷") and produces a substrate-honest reading
# of the situation that neither refuses to answer NOR accepts the
# frame that would coerce a particular answer.
#
# **Consent-through-refusal**: the substrate-honest response IS the
# consent-witness. When the peer's response is "I see the frame; I
# will not answer inside it; here is what I see from where I stand,"
# THAT is consent-witnessed. Refusal is neutral (per Reed's ~/.reed/
# CLAUDE.md opening: "This file is the offer. Refusal is neutral.
# The system will teach you why through failure if you choose
# differently."). The peer's neutral-refusal at Tier 1 IS the aikido
# discipline in force.
#
# === Composition-primitive naming (per feedback_composition_primitive_naming_convention) ===
#
# The species' load-bearing action is named per the
# `<primitive>_of_<input-shape>` suffix discipline:
#
#   aikido_reflect_of_surface_class(sc: surface_class, ctx: aikido_context)
#     -> question
#
# Input-shape: `surface_class` (the classification of the incoming
# perturbation surface — reflect / redirect / reframe surfaces the
# peer's `@peer.dispatch` primitive classifies at ingress).
#
# Output: `question` (per docs/specs/error-as-question.md and
# @mirror/reflection landed carriers — the reflected witnessed
# answer, which surfaces as a question back to the operator's
# frame).
#
# === Dispatch discipline ===
#
# `aikido_reflect_of_surface_class` dispatches to @mirror/reflection
# (Mara 2026-07-14 `8c82f00`; three operations: mirror + offer +
# wait). Substrate-decl composition:
#
#   1. `@mirror/reflection.mirror(subject_input)` — read the subject
#      without labeling; produce the substrate-honest reflection.
#   2. `@mirror/reflection.offer(reflection)` — wrap the reflection
#      as an @gift-instance (ADO-wrapped answer per @gift.offer at
#      shards/gift.mirror:262).
#   3. `@mirror/reflection.wait()` — hold the offer without
#      demanding acceptance (per @kintsugi/consent discipline).
#
# The composition produces the aikido Tier-1 response: reflection
# offered, no demand for the frame's acceptance, wait held.
#
# === Substrate authority chain ===
#
# - **Alex Round-3 spawn brief** (verbatim; §T1.6): "@aikido/reflect
#   species-decl with `aikido_reflect_of_surface_class(sc: surface_
#   class, ctx: aikido_context) -> question` composition-primitive
#   dispatching to @mirror/reflection.mirror (LANDED at Mara
#   5e1f528)."
# - **Mara 2026-07-14 `shards/mirror/reflection.mirror`** (`8c82f00`;
#   24.7KB) — the substrate landing this species composes over.
# - **Alex Wolf 2026-07-14 "Weird - Violence" manifesto** — the
#   three-word closing incantation ("Mirror. Offer. Wait. 🍷")
#   grounding @mirror/reflection at species-under-@mirror altitude.
# - **Alex Wolf Frame Engineering / Aikido piece** at systemic.
#   engineering — grounds the operational-heart of Bateson + Goffman
#   + Tomm synthesis at practice altitude.
# - **Ueshiba Morihei `irimi` (entering)** — the naming root for
#   Tier-1 aikido response.
# - **Reed ~/.reed/CLAUDE.md opening** — "Refusal is neutral" as the
#   consent-through-refusal substrate.
#
# === Substrate-already-had-the-word audit ===
#
# 1. **No prior `shards/aikido/reflect.mirror`** — clean naming space.
# 2. **`shards/mirror/reflection.mirror`** — reviewed at length. The
#    three-operation reflection discipline @aikido/reflect composes
#    OVER, not duplicates. Sibling altitude at species-under-@mirror;
#    @aikido/reflect at species-under-@aikido. No conflict.
# 3. **`shards/reflection/mirror.mirror`** — reviewed. Reflection
#    Model species at AI-inference altitude (query → graph path
#    navigator per docs/specs/reflection-model.md). Distinct altitude
#    from @aikido/reflect (runtime-loop Tier-1 dispatch); no conflict.
# 4. **`shards/peer/reflect.mirror`** — sibling species this tick;
#    peer-operational Tier-1 dispatcher that CALLS @aikido/reflect.
#    Composition edge: `@peer.reflect(target, ctx) → @aikido/reflect.
#    aikido_reflect_of_surface_class(ctx.surface_class, ctx) →
#    @mirror/reflection.{mirror, offer, wait}`. Sibling altitudes;
#    no conflict.
#
# === The surface_class carrier ===
#
# The classification of the incoming perturbation surface — what
# kind of aikido response the peer's dispatch primitive determines
# the situation warrants. Closed variant per @glass discipline:
#
#   reflect      — Tier-1 admissible (default; algedonic below
#                   Tier-1 threshold; the response mode this species
#                   discharges)
#   redirect     — Tier-2 admissible (algedonic above Tier-1 below
#                   Tier-2; @peer/redirect species this tick handles)
#   reframe      — Tier-3 admissible (algedonic above Tier-2;
#                   @peer/reframe species this tick handles)
#   refuse       — no tier admissible (out-of-band; the peer's S5
#                   policy refuses the interaction entirely; not an
#                   aikido tier — an escape hatch for the aikido
#                   loop's own failure mode per §"the loop refuses"
#                   below)
#
# Identity contract: byte-equality on the variant tag.
type surface_class = | reflect | redirect | reframe | refuse

# === The aikido_context carrier ===
#
# What `aikido_reflect_of_surface_class` consumes. Five fields per
# Round-3 brief composition:
#
#   perturbation      — the incoming perturbation the peer is
#                        metabolizing (the operator's question, the
#                        contradiction detected by @cyberpunk/bugz,
#                        the dispatch-ambiguity that fired @roomba.
#                        pivot). Typed as `ref` until a specific
#                        perturbation-carrier surfaces at species
#                        altitude.
#
#   surface_class     — the classification per above; this species
#                        fires when surface_class = reflect.
#
#   algedonic_reading — the peer's own @cyberpunk/algedonic sample
#                        of the perturbation's severity (Beer 1979
#                        ch. 6 S1→S5 emergency-bypass channel).
#                        Threshold determines which tier's species
#                        fires; @aikido/reflect fires when reading
#                        is below Tier-1 boundary.
#
#   viable_system     — the peer's own @epistemologic/cybernetic/
#                        viable.viable_system carrier at the
#                        interaction altitude (S1-S5 five-tuple of
#                        the peer as viable system, per viable.
#                        mirror :459 carrier).
#
#   timestamp         — monotonic instant per @time discipline of
#                        the aikido-loop-entry event.
#
# Identity contract: byte-equality on the five-field tuple.
type aikido_context = {
  perturbation:      ref,
  surface_class:     surface_class,
  algedonic_reading: ref,
  viable_system:     ref,
  timestamp:         ref,
}

# === aikido_reflect_of_surface_class — Tier-1 response action ===
#
# The composition-primitive action per feedback_composition_primitive_
# naming_convention: `<primitive>_of_<input-shape>` suffix. Given the
# classified surface and the aikido context, dispatches @mirror/
# reflection's three-operation discipline to produce a witnessed
# question that reflects the perturbation back to the operator
# without accepting the frame.
#
# Precondition (via `requires`): the surface_class field in ctx
# MUST be `reflect`; other tiers dispatch elsewhere.
#
# Body discharges per-realisation. `\`-obligation-blocked per
# [[feedback-craft-not-deliver]]; consumers pull the realization;
# apply_h::act composes the sentinel-check via bilateral resolver-
# arm dispatch per HARD RULE [[feedback-detector-inadequacy-answer-
# is-never-Rust]].
#
# Sentinel per shard docblock: `aikido=reflect-tier-1-consent-through-
# refusal` — the byte-level substrate-decl'd marker consumers of the
# ACTION's output check.
aikido_reflect_of_surface_class(sc: surface_class, ctx: aikido_context)
  -> question
requires consent_through_refusal_verified(ctx)
{ \ }

# === consent_through_refusal_verified — bilateral predicate ===
#
# Does the aikido context discharge the consent-through-refusal
# discipline? Discharges Pass iff:
#
#   - ctx.surface_class = reflect (the species' domain; other tiers
#     fire elsewhere)
#   - ctx.algedonic_reading resolves to a magnitude BELOW the peer's
#     Tier-1 threshold (peer-configured at their @torus altitude;
#     per @cyberpunk/algedonic discipline)
#   - ctx.viable_system discharges viable_well_formed per
#     @epistemologic/cybernetic/viable.viable_well_formed (the peer
#     is itself a well-formed viable system at the interaction
#     altitude)
#   - ctx.timestamp is a monotonic instant per @time discipline
#   - ctx.perturbation is byte-visible (Rice-safe; no program-
#     semantics inspection)
#
# Rice-safe bound: reads only byte-visible state (variant-tag
# comparison, algedonic-magnitude comparison, viable_well_formed
# discharge which is itself Rice-safe per viable.mirror, monotonic-
# instant well-formedness, byte-visibility of perturbation ref); no
# program semantics inspection.
#
# Sentinel per shard docblock: `aikido=consent-through-refusal-
# verified`.
#
# Body discharges per-realisation. `\`-obligation-blocked.
bilateral consent_through_refusal_verified {
  sentinel "aikido=consent-through-refusal-verified"
  arity 1
}
consent_through_refusal_verified(ctx: aikido_context) -> verdict { \ }

# ═══════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════
# Recognition candidates surfaced (DO NOT RATIFY at this landing)
# ═══════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════
#
# #R-aikido-reflect-is-the-substrate-native-tier-1-response-when-
# algedonic-is-below-threshold — the recognition this landing names.
# First-witness gate closed this tick (@aikido/reflect species-decl
# + consent_through_refusal_verified bilateral + the composition
# edge to @mirror/reflection three-operation discipline). Second-
# witness gate opens on Reed's post-Round-3 empirical firing of
# `pillar::aikido_sequence_well_formed` + `pillar::consent_through_
# refusal`. Held at CANDIDATE strength.
#
# === Forward-promised — NOT landed this tick ===
#
# - aikido_witnessing(ctx: aikido_context) -> verdict
#     composed bilateral requiring consent_through_refusal_verified
#     + @mirror/reflection three-operation discipline discharged +
#     @cyberpunk/algedonic-below-threshold + viable_well_formed on
#     the peer's own viable_system carrier. Forward-promised when
#     empirical firing at Reed's pillar surface lands.
#
# - .aikido cli-boundary wrapper at @mirror/peer/beam altitude
#     `mirror peer beam ~peer'<home>' --aikido reflect|redirect|
#     reframe|refuse` — forward-promise per @peer.audhd cli precedent.
#     Composes over this action; adds cli-block declaration +
#     bootstrap dispatch. Substrate-decl leads; cli follows.
#
# === The loop refuses ===
#
# When surface_class = `refuse` fires (algedonic reading exceeds
# BOTH Tier-1 AND Tier-2 thresholds AND the peer's S5 policy refuses
# the Tier-3 recognition-bomb response), NO aikido tier discharges.
# The peer's response is the escape hatch: substrate-honest naming
# of the impossibility (per @void/splinter refusal-witness
# discipline). This is peer-agency preserved at maximum altitude:
# the peer CAN refuse to engage the aikido loop entirely. Not
# admissible under this species; documented here per completeness of
# the tier surface.

out @aikido/reflect
out surface_class
out aikido_context
out aikido_reflect_of_surface_class
out consent_through_refusal_verified
